{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature.md","line":158,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature.tex#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness","line":510,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[backward uniqueness of Jacobi fields]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal, def:dc-ch5-2-1}\n\n  A Jacobi field along a geodesic on $[a,b]$ with $J(b)=0$ and $DJ(b)=0$ vanishes identically\n  on $[a,b]$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch\n  Reverse time using \\cref{lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal}. The reversed pair has zero\n  initial data at $-b$, so forward uniqueness makes it, and hence the original pair, zero.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[backward uniqueness of Jacobi fields] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368382d322d312d6a61636f62692d6261636b776172642d756e697175656e657373\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_JacobiFields%23def%3Adc-ch5-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch5-2-1</a> <p></p>A Jacobi field along a geodesic on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[a,b]$\">$[a,b]$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J(b)=0$\">$J(b)=0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$DJ(b)=0$\">$DJ(b)=0$</span> vanishes identically on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[a,b]$\">$[a,b]$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Reverse time using <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368382d322d312d6a61636f62692d726576657273616c\">section 1</a>. The reversed pair has zero initial data at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$-b$\">$-b$</span>, so forward uniqueness makes it, and hence the original pair, zero. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch5-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch5-2-1"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#thm:dc-ch8-2-1","title":"thm:dc-ch8-2-1","label":"thm:dc-ch8-2-1"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[backward uniqueness of Jacobi fields]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal, def:dc-ch5-2-1}\n\n  A Jacobi field along a geodesic on $[a,b]$ with $J(b)=0$ and $DJ(b)=0$ vanishes identically\n  on $[a,b]$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch\n  Reverse time using \\cref{lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal}. The reversed pair has zero\n  initial data at $-b$, so forward uniqueness makes it, and hence the original pair, zero.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch5-2-1","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}